TOKEN tinybird_read READ

DESCRIPTION >
    Estimated price of one agent call, per agent.

    A managed agent turns one request into several generations - model steps and
    MCP tool calls - each authenticated with the run token minted for the parent
    request. Every one of those carries `parent_request_id`, so grouping by it
    reassembles a single agent call. The parent row itself is always free, so a
    run's cost is exactly the sum over its children and the parent never needs
    to be read.

    Reported as median and p90 rather than a mean: a run that enters a tool loop
    costs a multiple of one that answers directly, and an average hides that.

NODE runs
DESCRIPTION >
    One row per agent call. Non-final rows are fallback attempts that never
    carry price, so excluding them keeps `calls` a count of generations rather
    than of attempts.
SQL >
    %
    SELECT
        agent_id,
        parent_request_id,
        sum(total_price) AS run_price,
        count() AS calls
    FROM generation_event_v2
    WHERE
        parent_request_id != ''
        AND is_final
        AND environment = {{String(environment, 'production')}}
        AND start_time >= now() - INTERVAL {{Int32(days, 7)}} DAY
        {% if defined(agent_id) %}
        AND agent_id = {{String(agent_id)}}
        {% end %}
    GROUP BY agent_id, parent_request_id

NODE endpoint
SQL >
    SELECT
        agent_id,
        count() AS runs,
        round(median(run_price), 6) AS median_price,
        round(quantile(0.9)(run_price), 6) AS p90_price,
        round(avg(run_price), 6) AS avg_price,
        round(avg(calls), 2) AS avg_calls
    FROM runs
    GROUP BY agent_id
    ORDER BY runs DESC
